Great question 👍 – WordPress runs fine with just the PHP core, but enabling the right extensions can significantly improve performance, caching, and scalability. Let me break it down from your list:
________________________________________
🔑 Must-have performance boosters for WordPress
1.	opcache – Critical.
•	Compiles and caches PHP bytecode in memory → faster page loads, lower CPU usage.
•	This is the #1 performance extension for WordPress.
2.	apcu – Object caching.
•	Provides fast in-memory object caching for PHP.
•	Can speed up WordPress (especially with plugins like W3 Total Cache, LiteSpeed Cache, or object-cache.php drop-ins).
3.	memcache / memcached or redis – Persistent caching.
•	Use one of these for database query caching, transients, and object caching.
•	Redis is often preferred in 2025 (better support + stability).
4.	igbinary – Serialization performance boost.
•	Works with APCu, Memcached, Redis for faster object storage.
•	Optional but recommended if using object caching.
5.	brotli and zlib/zip – Compression.
•	Brotli or gzip compression reduces asset sizes sent to the browser.
•	Helps with front-end performance (Core Web Vitals).
________________________________________
📊 Other useful ones
•	mbstring – Required by WordPress core and many plugins for string handling.
•	intl – Better internationalization, sorting, formatting. Important for multilingual sites.
•	imagick or gd – Efficient image handling (resizing, compression, thumbnails).
•	curl – Needed for API requests, plugin/theme updates.
•	json – Essential for REST API.
•	mysqli / pdo_mysql / mysqlnd – Database connectivity. mysqlnd is preferred.
________________________________________
🚫 Not directly performance-related
Modules like calendar, bz2, ldap, imap, soap, snmp, xmlrpc, ssh2, etc., don’t really improve WordPress performance. They’re more for specific features or integrations.
________________________________________
✅ In summary, to improve performance enable:
•	opcache
•	apcu
•	redis or memcached (choose one)
•	igbinary (optional but nice)
•	brotli or zlib
•	mbstring, intl, imagick/gd, curl, json, mysqli/mysqlnd
________________________________________
