8 — Sync Strategy (ready for future backend)
•	Local change queue: audit_logs hold operations {op, store, payload, timestamp, id}.
•	When network available:
•	Read unsynced logs and POST to sync endpoint /sync/changes.
•	Receive ack mapping localIds -> serverIds (store in meta).
•	Resolve conflicts by last-writer-wins or server-authoritative rules.
•	Pull updates: polling or long-poll to fetch authoritative content deltas from server.
For now, implement sync stubs that simulate successful push and set pendingSync=false.
________________________________________
9 — Security & Sensitive Data Handling
•	Do not store passwords or tokens in IndexedDB in cleartext. For demo, use no-auth or local pin.
•	Never store bank details or sensitive PII client-side. If required later, integrate OAuth & token store on server.
•	Use client-side encryption for any sensitive blob stored locally (Crypto Subtle).
•	Use HTTPS when deploying PWA assets.
________________________________________
10 — File Storage & Sizes
•	Browsers impose storage quotas by origin; usage varies by device. Keep files small:
•	Use thumbnails and short video placeholders (or link to external YouTube).
•	For file uploads, allow only small files (≤ 5–10MB depending on device).
•	Provide export to cloud/manual backup option.
________________________________________
11 — Migration to Backend (future)
•	When ready to add server:
•	Implement /sync endpoints to accept audit_logs.
•	Server returns canonical resources and conflict resolution decisions.
•	Migrate local IDs to server IDs using mapping table in meta store.
•	Add auth using JWT and secure refresh tokens; keep only tokens in memory or secure cookies (do NOT store refresh tokens client-side unless encrypted).
