Cyber Elias Academy — Functional Requirements Document (FRD)
Version: 1.0
This FRD translates the PRD into detailed functional behaviors, UI screens, flows, API contracts, data models, and test cases.
________________________________________
1. System Overview & Architecture (high level)
Architecture pattern: 3-tier microservices-ready architecture.
•	Frontend: React (Next.js) — SSR for public pages, client rendering for LMS; Tailwind CSS; Framer Motion animations; PWA.
•	Backend (API): Node.js (NestJS or Express) or Python (FastAPI). RESTful + GraphQL option for heavy data.
•	Database: PostgreSQL (primary relational data). Redis for session & cache. Elasticsearch for search.
•	Media: Cloudinary/Mux for media hosting; S3 (object storage) for file backups.
•	Auth: OAuth2 + JWT for API; social login (Google, Facebook).
•	Queue/Jobs: RabbitMQ or AWS SQS for background tasks (certificate generation, emails).
•	Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana, Sentry for errors.
•	CI/CD: GitHub Actions / GitLab CI; Docker images; Terraform for infra.
Diagram (developer copy): Frontend ↔ API Gateway ↔ Microservices (Auth, LMS, Payments, Jobs, Admin) ↔ PostgreSQL/Redis/Elasticsearch; Media ↔ Cloud Storage; Queue for background processing.
________________________________________
2. User Roles & Permissions (RBAC)
•	Guest: view public pages, blog.
•	Student: enroll in courses, take quizzes, submit assignments, apply for jobs.
•	Instructor: create courses, lessons, grade assignments, host live sessions.
•	SME Client: post projects, request SME services, hire talent.
•	Mentor: limited instructor rights for mentorship.
•	Admin: global access, user management, content approval, billing, compliance.
•	Finance: access to billing and refunds.
•	Support: respond to tickets, moderate community.
Each endpoint must check role scope using middleware. Fine-grained permissions for content (instructor can only edit their courses unless admin).
________________________________________
3. Detailed Functional Modules
3.1 Authentication & User Management
Features
•	Sign up / sign in with email & password.
•	Phone OTP verification (via SMS provider).
•	Social login (Google).
•	Password reset & recovery.
•	2FA (optional via TOTP for instructor/admin).
•	Profile management (name, photo, bio, skills, CV upload).
•	KYC flow (for agency freelancers & SME onboarding) — upload ID, CAC docs for company accounts.
APIs
•	POST /api/auth/register — payload {name, email, phone, password, role} → returns user + token (email verification required).
•	POST /api/auth/login — returns JWT & refresh token.
•	POST /api/auth/otp/send — for phone verification.
•	POST /api/auth/reset — password reset flow.
Validation & Constraints
•	Password strength policy (min 10 chars, uppercase, number).
•	Emails unique; username slug unique.
________________________________________
3.2 Public Marketing Site / CMS
Features
•	Landing pages editable via admin CMS (title, hero banner, CTA).
•	Blog with categories, SEO fields (meta title, meta desc), tags.
•	SEO-friendly URLs and sitemap generation.
•	Static rendering for SEO (Next.js SSG/SSR).
APIs
•	GET /api/pages/:slug
•	GET /api/posts (pagination, filters)
•	Admin CRUD endpoints for pages & posts.
Acceptance
•	Each page loads with correct meta tags, images optimized, mobile-friendly.
________________________________________
3.3 Course & Content Management (LMS)
Entities: Course, Syllabus, Module, Lesson, Quiz, Assignment, Resource, Category, Tag.
Course object fields (example)
•	id, title, slug, shortDescription, fullDescription, instructorId, price, currency, level, duration, categories[], tags[], thumbnailUrl, videoIntroUrl, published (bool), createdAt, updatedAt.
Lesson
•	id, courseId, title, order, contentType (video/article/quiz), contentUrl, contentHTML, duration, attachments[].
Quizzes
•	Question list, types (MCQ, multi-select, fill-in), points, timers, passingScore.
Assignments
•	File uploads, dueDate, auto/manual grading, feedback comments.
Flows
•	Instructor creates course → saves in draft → uploads lessons (video to media provider) → publishes.
•	Student views catalog → enroll (pay or free) → course appears in “My Courses” dashboard → progress tracked per lesson → upon completion and passing quizzes, certificate is generated.
APIs (selected)
•	GET /api/courses — filter by category, search, pagination.
•	GET /api/courses/:id — course detail.
