ients/Employers: Businesses/NGOs hiring talent or services. Admins/Core Staff: 3-5 initial users managing ops (Director, Ops Manager, Tech Lead, etc.). Community Partners: NGOs, schools for bootcamps. Alumni: For ongoing mentorship and gigs. Key Outcomes:80% student retention via gamified learning. 70% employment placement within 6 months. 20% profit margin on services. Scalable to 1,000+ users nationally (Phase 3). Business Alignment: Directly maps to revenue streams (tuitions, subscriptions, hiring fees, grants). Automates 80% of SOPs (e.g., student registration → payments → certificates). Success Metrics (KPIs):User Engagement: Daily active users (DAU) >50% of registered. Conversion: 20% lead-to-enrollment. Uptime: 99%. Revenue per User: ₦50K/student lifecycle. 1.2 User Personas and StoriesPersona 1: Student (e.g., 22-year-old Nigerian undergrad).Story: "As a student, I want to enroll in a web dev course, access modules offline, submit projects, get certified, and find freelance gigs so I can earn while learning." Persona 2: Employer/Client.Story: "As a business owner, I want to browse talent profiles, post job/project needs, hire freelancers, and pay via app to fill tech gaps quickly." Persona 3: Admin (Ops Manager).Story: "As an admin, I want dashboards for tracking enrollments, finances, and projects to run the academy with minimal staff." Persona 4: Community Partner.Story: "As an NGO, I want to schedule bootcamps, access free resources, and sponsor students to empower rural areas." 1.3 High-Level FeaturesPrioritized for MVP (Minimum Viable Product) in lean phase:Student Portal: Profile, courses, assignments, progress tracking. Course Library: Modules, videos, quizzes, projects. Payments & Certifications: Secure transactions, auto-certificates. Job Board & Talent Marketplace: Postings, profiles, hiring. Project Management: For internal/client projects (task assignment, supervision). Community Forums: Discussions, events, bootcamps. ERP Dashboards: Finance, HR, Ops, Marketing analytics. Admin Tools: User management, reporting, automation triggers. Non-Functional: Offline access (via PWA), multi-language (English + Pidgin hints), accessibility (WCAG compliant).1.4 RoadmapMVP (Phase 1, 3 months): Core LMS + basic job board + payments. Built with low-code (Bubble.io) for speed. V1.1 (Phase 2): Add ERP + marketplace. V2 (Phase 3): National scaling with AI features (e.g., auto-grading). Dependencies: Integrate with existing tools (e.g., Google Workspace for auth). 1.5 Risks and AssumptionsRisks: Low adoption → Mitigate with free trials. Data privacy (GDPR/Nigeria DPA compliant). Assumptions: Users have basic smartphones; internet redundancy via app caching. 2. Functional Requirements Document (FRD)Detailed specs for each feature, broken into sub-atomic components (e.g., user flows, inputs/outputs, validation rules).2.1 User Authentication and RolesFunctional Req 1.1: Registration/Login.Flow: User enters email/phone → OTP verification (via Twilio) → Profile setup (name, skills map from curriculum). Roles: Student (read courses), Instructor (upload content), Client (post jobs), Admin (full access). Validation: Email unique; Password 8+ chars with symbols. Output: JWT token for sessions. Req 1.2: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).Student: View own progress, forums. Admin: Edit all, view dashboards. Edge Case: Inactive user (no login 30 days) → Auto-email reminder. 2.2 Student PortalReq 2.1: Profile Management.Components: Edit bio, skills badges (e.g., "HTML Mastery"), portfolio upload (GitHub links, PDFs). Flow: Upload project → Auto-add to talent database. Granularity: Skills broken into atoms (e.g., HTML: Semantic tags, Accessibility checks). Req 2.2: Course Enrollment.Flow: Browse library → Select course (e.g., Full-Stack Web Dev) → Pay tuition (Paystack integration) → Auto-access modules. Validation: Pre-reqs (e.g., Basic IT for AI course). Output: Enrollment ID, calendar sync. 2.3 Course Library and Learning SystemReq 3.1: Module Delivery.Structure: Course → Modules (e.g., Web Dev: HTML) → Lessons (videos/text) → Tasks (code exercises) → Projects (clone website) → Mastery Checks (quizzes). Flow: Progressive unlock (complete 80% to advance). Offline: Cache videos via Service Workers. Granularity: Lesson atoms: Video (5-min chunks), Transcript (auto-generated via Whisper API if integrated), Quiz (multiple-choice, code snippets). Req 3.2: Assignments and Feedback.Flow: Submit code/file → Auto-grade (e.g., via CodeSandbox integration) → Mentor review (comments, ratings). Validation: Plagiarism check (simple string match). Output: Feedback loop: Score + suggestions. 2.4 Payments and CertificationsReq 4.1: Payment Processing.Flow: Cart (courses/bootcamps) → Checkout → Paystack redirect → Webhook confirm → Update status. Types: Tuition (one-time), Subscriptions (monthly access), Hiring fees (5% commission). Granularity: Currency (NGN/USD), Refunds (admin-approved, 7-day window). Req 4.2: Certification Issuance.Flow: 100% mastery → Auto-generate PDF (with QR code for verification) → Email + profile badge. Validation: Blockchain hash for tamper-proof (optional in V2). 2.5 Job Board and Talent MarketplaceReq 5.1: Talent Profiles.Components: Searchable DB (skills, experience, rates). Flow: Student builds → Auto-populate from courses/projects. Req 5.2: Job Postings and Hiring.Flow: Employer posts (title, skills needed, budget) → Matches via algo (keyword + score) → Applications → Interviews (in-app chat/video). Granularity: Atoms: Bid system (freelance), Contracts (e-sign via DocuSign API), Payouts (escrow, 70/30 split). Req 5.3: Freelance Incubation.Flow: Profile setup wizard → Pitch templates → Internal gigs routing. 2.6 Project ManagementReq 6.1: Client Project Workflow.Flow: Inquiry form → Proposal generator → Task board (Kanban: ToDo/InProgress/Done) → Assign to students → QA checklist. Integration: Trello embed or custom (columns for Requirement Analysis → Execution → Delivery). Granularity: Task atoms: Sub-tasks (e.g., Code HTML), Time tracking (auto-log), Comments. 2.7 Community Forums and EmpowermentReq 7.1: Forums.Components: Threads (Q&A, discussions), Moderation (flag/spam detection). Flow: Post → Replies → Upvotes. Req 7.2: Event Management.Flow: Schedule bootcamp → RSVPs → Mobile lab tracking (GPS if integrated). Granularity: Sponsorship atoms: Grant applications form, Impact reports (attendees trained). 2.8 ERP DashboardsReq 8.1: Financial Dashboard.Views: Revenue tracking (per course), Expenses, Cashflow forecast (charts via Chart.js). Flow: Auto-pull from payments → Generate reports (PDF export). Req 8.2: HR/Operations.Components: Staff onboarding forms, Attendance logs (biometric if V2), Asset management (equipment QR scans). Req 8.3: Sales/Marketing.Flow: Lead CRM (HubSpot sync) → Campaign builder → Analytics (conversion rates). 2.9 Automation and IntegrationsReq 9.1: Triggers.Examples: Enrollment → Slack notify admin; Project complete → Invoice auto-send. Tools: Zapier for no-code automations. 3. Technical Design3.1 Overall ArchitectureMonolithic MVP → Microservices for Scale: Start monolithic (Bubble.io for rapid dev), evolve to microservices (e.g., User Service, Learning Service). Stack: MERN (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js) or low-code (Bubble.io/Adalo) for lean. Deployment: Heroku/AWS free tier → Scalable EC2. Data Flow: Frontend → API Gateway → Backend Services → DB → External (e.g., Paystack). Security: HTTPS, JWT auth, Rate limiting, Input sanitization (OWASP top 10 compliant). Scaling Mechanics: Horizontal (add servers), Caching (Redis), CDN for media. 3.2 Backend DesignDatabase Schema (MongoDB):Users Collection: {_id, email, role, profile: {skills: [{name: "HTML", level: 80}], portfolio: [links]}}. Courses Collection: {_id, name: "Web Dev", modules: [{id, lessons: [{videoUrl, quiz: [{question, answers}]}]}]}. Projects Collection: {_id, clientId, tasks: [{assignee, status, subtasks: [{description, deadline}]}]}. Payments Collection: {_id, userId, amount, status, transactionId (from Paystack)}. Jobs Collection: {_id, title, skillsRequired: ["AI"], bids: [{userId, amount}]}. Granularity: Indexes on skills for fast search; Nested docs for atomic modules. APIs (RESTful + GraphQL for complex queries):Endpoint Example: /api/enroll/course/:id (POST): Body {userId, paymentToken} → Validate → Update user progress → Return enrollment. Sub-Atomic: Query Params (e.g., ?filter=completed for progress). Error Handling: Standard codes (400 bad request), Logs (Winston). Code Snippet (Node.js): app.post('/api/enroll/course/:id', authenticate, async (req, res) => { try { const course = await Course.findById(req.params.id); if (!course) return res.status(404).json({error: 'Course not found'}); // Paystack verify const payment = await paystack.verify(req.body.transactionId); if (payment.status) { await User.updateOne({_id: req.user.id}, {$push: {enrollments: {courseId: course._id, progress: 0}}}); res.json({success: true}); } } catch (err) { res.status(500).json({error: err.message}); } }); 3.3 Frontend DesignFramework: React.js with Redux for state (or Bubble.io UI builder). Pages/Screens:Dashboard: Personalized (student: Progress bars; admin: KPI charts). Course Page: Tabs (Modules, Assignments) → Accordion for lessons (expand to video player). Job Board: Search bar (filters: skills, location) → Cards (job details, apply button). Project Kanban: Drag-drop tasks (React Beautiful DnD). Granularity: Components: <SkillBadge level={80} /> (SVG icon + tooltip), <QuizQuestion options={['A', 'B']} onSubmit={handleAnswer} />. UI/UX Flows:Enrollment: Modal popup → Stepper (1. Select, 2. Pay, 3. Confirm). Offline: Sync queue (e.g., submit assignment when back online). Accessibility: ARIA labels, Keyboard nav. 3.4 Integration and Automation StackMapped from Previous: Bubble.io (core), Zapier (triggers), Paystack (payments), Google Auth (login), Twilio (OTP), Slack (notifications). Granular Automations: If user completes module → Zapier: Update progress DB → Send certificate email → Post to forum "Congrats!". Testing: Unit (Jest for components), Integration (Postman for APIs), E2E (Cypress for flows). 3.5 Security and ComplianceAuth: OAuth2, 2FA for admins. Data Protection: Encrypt sensitive (PII in DB), Audit logs for actions. Edge Cases: SQL injection prevention (Mongoose sanitization), DDoS (Cloudflare). 3.6 Performance and ScalingOptimizations: Lazy loading modules, Compression (Gzip). Stress-Test Mapping: Surge (100 enrolls): Auto-scale DB replicas. Turnover: API docs for easy handover. Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana for metrics (e.g., API response time <200ms). This design ensures the app is a self-sustaining organism, aligning every atom (e.g., a quiz question) to business goals like revenue stability and student success. create an implementation roadmap that covers every single thing about building this app, from scratch to production readiness, everything must cover even tiniest implementation tasks, subtask, sub-atomically granular task steps and every possible thing needed to be done to make the app fully implemented and actually work to full operation 


