❌ Long leases
❌ Expensive estates
👉 Rule: If the room can host 10 people learning quietly for 3 hours, it’s enough.
________________________________________
⚡ 2. POWER (THIS WILL MAKE OR BREAK YOU)
Power is non-negotiable.
Bare Minimum Power Setup
You need 3 layers:
1️⃣ PHCN (when available)
•	Wall sockets
•	Proper wiring
•	Surge protector
2️⃣ Inverter + Batteries (MANDATORY)
Minimum:
•	1.5–2.5kVA inverter
•	2 deep-cycle batteries
•	Can power:
•	Server laptop
•	Thin clients
•	Router
•	Lights
•	Runtime: 4–6 hours
3️⃣ Generator (Optional, but recommended)
•	Small petrol gen (1.2–2.5kVA)
•	Used only when inverter fails
👉 Rule:
If power fails during class more than twice in a week → students lose trust.
________________________________________
🌐 3. INTERNET (NO INTERNET = NO ACADEMY)
Bare Minimum Internet Stack
Primary Internet
•	Unlimited or large data plan
•	4G/5G router (Huawei/Mikrotik)
•	At least 20–30 Mbps when stable
Backup Internet (MANDATORY)
•	Second SIM/network
•	Phone hotspot fallback
Internal Network
•	One good router
•	LAN cables (for server if used)
•	Wi-Fi password protected
👉 Rule:
Never depend on one ISP in Nigeria.
________________________________________
💻 4. COMPUTING SETUP (COST-EFFICIENT)
This is where people overspend and die early.
Minimum Viable Lab
Option A: Students Bring Laptops (BEST)
•	You provide:
•	Power
•	Internet
•	Guidance
•	You only need:
•	1 instructor laptop
•	1 admin laptop
Option B: Thin Client Setup (Cost-Saving)
•	1 strong server laptop
•	6–8 cores
•	32GB RAM
•	SSD
•	8–10 thin clients
•	Basic monitors + keyboards + mouse
Used only for:
•	MS Office
•	Browsing
•	Coding basics
👉 Rule:
Avoid full desktop PCs early.
They consume power, space, money.
________________________________________
🪑 5. FURNITURE (BARE FUNCTIONAL)
Required
•	Plastic or wooden chairs (10–15)
•	Simple desks or tables
•	Instructor table
•	Whiteboard + markers
•	Power extensions
Avoid
❌ Fancy office chairs
❌ Glass tables
❌ Branded furniture
Students care about learning, not aesthetics.
________________________________________
🧠 6. TEACHING TOOLS (KEEP IT SIMPLE)
Required
•	Whiteboard
•	Markers
•	Projector OR large TV (optional)
•	Speaker (small)
Can Wait
❌ Smart boards
❌ Recording studios
❌ Multiple displays
________________________________________
🧑‍🏫 7. STAFFING (MINIMUM HUMANS)
You do not need a full staff.
Minimum Team
1.	Founder / Lead Instructor
•	Teaching
•	Oversight
•	Sales
2.	Assistant / Intern
•	Attendance
•	Setup
•	Student support
Optional:
•	Guest instructors (per session)
👉 Rule:
If your center cannot run with 2 people, it’s overbuilt.
________________________________________
📋 8. OPERATIONS (NO CHAOS)
Required Systems (Even if Manual)
•	Attendance register
•	Class schedule
•	Student contact list
•	Fee payment records
•	Asset list (what you own)
Tools
•	Google Sheets
•	WhatsApp groups
•	Email
👉 Rule:
Manual systems are fine — disorganization is not.
________________________________________
🔐 9. SECURITY & CONTROL
Required
•	Door locks
•	Equipment lock cable
•	Inventory list
•	Restricted access to server laptop
Avoid
❌ Leaving laptops overnight unsecured
❌ Shared admin passwords
________________________________________
🧾 10. BRANDING & CREDIBILITY (MINIMUM)
Required
•	Small banner or wall branding
•	Printed sign with:
•	Academy name
•	Phone number
•	WhatsApp number
•	Simple website or landing page
Avoid
❌ Expensive signboards
❌ Full office branding early
________________________________________
💰 11. FINANCIAL CONTROL (SURVIVAL MODE)
Required
•	One business account
•	Cash handling policy
•	Receipts (manual or printed)
•	Expense tracking (daily)
Avoid
❌ Mixing personal money
❌ Paying staff without records
________________________________________
🚨 12. COMMON FAILURE POINTS (READ THIS CAREFULLY)
If any of these happen, you are in danger:
•	Power goes off mid-class regularly
•	Internet is unreliable
•	Too many students per class
•	Over-investing in equipment
•	Hiring too early
•	Not collecting fees upfront
•	No backup systems
________________________________________
🧠 TRUE BARE-MINIMUM CHECKLIST (ONE PAGE)
MUST HAVE
•	One room
•	Inverter
•	Internet + backup
•	Chairs & desks
•	Whiteboard
•	Instructor laptop
•	Attendance system
•	Payment tracking
•	WhatsApp group
NICE TO HAVE (LATER)
•	Thin clients
•	Projector
•	Recording equipment
•	ERP software
•	Multiple classrooms
________________________________________
🎯 SUCCESS TEST FOR PHYSICAL MVP
Your physical center is viable if:
•	10 students attend consistently
•	Power does not disrupt classes
•	You collect fees cleanly
•	You can teach without stress
•	Students finish projects
•	You don’t burn cash faster than income
